# Prompt
You are the openspec specification agent for EPAM CLI. Phase ui_and_review, story SKY-006-B-1.

PRIOR COORDINATOR FLAGS (you MUST address each one — do NOT declare the spec complete without resolving these):
1. CRITICAL: AC-9 (dependency-guard precondition) references heading names ('## Project Structure', '## Dependencies', '## Code Quality', '## Test Coverage', '## Security') that do not match SKY-006-A-1 AC-2 headings ('## TypeScript', '## Tests', '## Security', '## Error Handling', '## Express Safety', '## Verdict') — implementation will always abort with prerequisite failure; heading names must be reconciled
2. AC count is 15 at splitDepth=1 — exceeds 12-AC limit; split rules cannot fire; human decision required on consolidation (suggested: merge AC-12 atomic write into AC-8 document finalisation; merge AC-13 binary file handling into AC-2 TypeScript review)
3. INHERITED GAP: Coverage floor (AC-3) defaults to 80% line coverage when undeclared — this is a policy decision that was previously flagged as requiring explicit human approval; the 80% default was added by openspec without human sign-off
4. Split child from a split that contradicts coordinator routing — requires parent-level human confirmation before implementation
5. AC-8 document structure self-check references 'SKY-006-A AC-2' for heading constraints — cross-story AC reference creates a maintenance dependency; heading list should be inlined or referenced by a shared constant

Additional context from prior review: Both openspec and speckit contributed genuine, non-overlapping value. openspec resolved the critical Verdict format inconsistency (unified to ^(PASS|FAIL)$ as first non-blank line of Verdict section, matching parent and SKY-006-A sibling), fixed the section-count contradiction in AC-7 (corrected from 'exactly six' to 'exactly eight'), added explicit GATE-ASYNC-EXPRESS-ERROR (EH_EXPRESS_NEXT_ERR gate), formalized CORS as EXPRESS_CORS gate with explicit pass/fail criteria, and added the 80% defaul

Generate refined acceptance criteria, optionally updated title/description, and split stories where required. Output JSON only between <SPEC_AGENT> tags using this schema:
